  "security_implications": "Lifecycle debug enable (lc_hw_debug_en) and DFT enable (lc_dft_en) signals directly gate hardware debug features. Incorrect synchronization, invalid multi-bit encodings, or missing gating (lc_hw_debug_en_gated_raw) could allow unauthorized debug access, exposing all system secrets, register state, and memory. testmode derived from scanmode_i may enable scan chains; any weakness in mubi4 testing could open a scan-based attack surface. The OTP late-debug disable signal (otp_dis_rv_dm_late_debug) prevents debug on production devices; corruption of its mubi8 code could silently re-enable debug. Enum width miscalculation tied to NrHarts could alias debug request encodings, bypassing lifecycle arbitration.",
  "evidence_refs": [
    "/home/smy/opentitan/hw/ip/rv_dm/rtl/rv_dm.sv:177-178",
